---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="DreamMeaningGuide — Explore the Symbols of Your Dreams"
  description="Discover the hidden meanings behind your dreams. Explore symbols, archetypes, and the unconscious mind with DreamMeaningGuide.site."
>
  <style>
    .hero {
      text-align: center;
      padding: 6rem 2rem 4rem;
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .hero-glyph {
      font-size: 5rem;
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      filter: drop-shadow(0 0 32px rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.5));
      animation: float 6s ease-in-out infinite;
    }
    @keyframes float {
      0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }
      50% { transform: translateY(-12px); }
    }
    h1 {
      font-family: 'Cinzel', serif;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      color: #d8c8ff;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }
    .tagline {
      font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
      color: #a78bfa;
      font-weight: 300;
      max-width: 600px;
      margin: 0 auto 3rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    /* OG image styling */
    .og-image {
      max-width: 420px;
      width: 100%;
      margin: 2rem auto 3rem;
      display: block;
      border-radius: 12px;
      box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.25);
    }

    .nav-cards {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr));
      gap: 1.25rem;
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 1.5rem 5rem;
    }
    .nav-card {
      background: rgba(45, 21, 84, 0.55);
      border: 1px solid rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.18);
      border-radius: 1.25rem;
      padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
      text-align: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: #e8e0ff;
      transition: all 0.22s ease;
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .nav-card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-5px);
      box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.25);
      border-color: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.4);
    }
    .card-icon { font-size: 2.5rem; }
    .card-title { font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #c4b5fd; }
    .card-desc { font-size: 0.85rem; color: #a78bfa; line-height: 1.6; }

    /* FAQ styling */
    .faqs {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto 4rem;
      padding: 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .faqs h2 {
      font-family: 'Cinzel', serif;
      font-size: 2rem;
      color: #d8c8ff;
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    details {
      background: rgba(45, 21, 84, 0.55);
      border: 1px solid rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.18);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    }
    summary {
      font-family: 'Cinzel', serif;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      color: #c4b5fd;
    }
    details p {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      color: #e8e0ff;
      line-height: 1.6;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  </style>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="hero">
    <span class="hero-glyph">✦</span>
    <h1>Explore the Symbols<br/>of Your Dreams</h1>
    <p class="tagline">
      Dreams carry meaning. DreamMeaningGuide helps you decode the symbols,
      archetypes, and patterns your unconscious mind leaves behind.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- OG IMAGE ABOVE NAV CARDS -->
<img 
  src="/og-default.png" 
  alt="DreamMeaningGuide Symbolic Preview" 
  class="og-image"
  style="max-width: 720px; width: 100%; margin: 2rem auto 3rem; display: block;"
/>

  <!-- NAV CARDS (About removed) -->
  <div class="nav-cards">
    <a href="/dream-symbols" class="nav-card">
      <span class="card-icon">🌀</span>
      <span class="card-title">Dream Symbols</span>
      <span class="card-desc">Browse animals, places, emotions, and archetypes and their deeper meanings.</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/seer" class="nav-card">
      <span class="card-icon">🔮</span>
      <span class="card-title">The Seer</span>
      <span class="card-desc">Ask a question and receive a symbolic answer from the oracle within.</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/journal" class="nav-card">
      <span class="card-icon">📖</span>
      <span class="card-title">Dream Journal</span>
      <span class="card-desc">Record your dreams, receive reflections, and build your personal archive.</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/sleep-tools" class="nav-card">
      <span class="card-icon">🌙</span>
      <span class="card-title">Sleep Tools Hub</span>
      <span class="card-desc">Curated tools for deeper sleep, richer dreams, and meaningful rest.</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <!-- FAQ SECTION -->
  <section class="faqs">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details>
      <summary>How do you navigate the site and the Dream Symbols page?</summary>
      <p>
        The site is organized into symbolic chambers. The Dream Symbols page is your reference library —  
        browse categories like Animals, Archetypes, Emotions, and Places, or search for a specific symbol.  
        Each symbol page offers a clear interpretation to help you understand what your dreams are communicating.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What is the Guides page for?</summary>
      <p>
        Guides are long‑form articles that explore dream meaning, symbolism, sleep science, and the inner life.  
        They function like blog posts — timeless, reflective pieces designed to deepen your understanding  
        of dreams and the symbolic world.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What is The Seer?</summary>
      <p>
        The Seer is your symbolic companion — a reflective tool that helps you explore meaning in dreams,  
        relationships, and life events. Ask The Seer about a dream, a symbol, or a situation, and it will  
        offer insight drawn from archetypes, patterns, and emotional symbolism.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How does the Dream Journal work?</summary>
      <p>
        The Dream Journal lets you record dreams directly in your browser — no login required.  
        Entries are saved locally on your device, creating a private archive of your dream life.  
        Soon, DreamMeaningGuide will offer pattern analysis across weeks and months, helping you  
        discover recurring symbols, emotional themes, and long‑term dream cycles.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>





